          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s104",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "אֵל בָּרוּךְ גְּדוֹל דֵּעָה. הֵכִין וּפָעַל זָהֳרֵי חַמָּה. טוֹב יָצַר כָּבוֹד לִשְׁמוֹ. מְאוֹרוֹת נָתַן סְבִיבוֹת עֻזּוֹ. פִּנּוֹת צְבָאָיו קְדוֹשִׁים רוֹמְמֵי שַׁדָּי. תָּמִיד מְסַפְּרִים כְּבוֹד־אֵל וּקְדֻשָּׁתוֹ: תִּתְבָּרַךְ יְיָ אֱלֹהֵינוּ עַל־שֶֽׁבַח מַעֲשֵׂה יָדֶֽיךָ. וְעַל־מְאוֹרֵי־אוֹר שֶׁעָשִׂיתָ יְפָאֲרוּךָ סֶּֽלָה:",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s105",
                "printed_page": "38",
                "text": "Blessed God, great in knowledge, He has prepared and made the sun’s rays, the Benevolent has fashioned glory for His Name, lights has He placed around His might, the chiefs of His hosts are holy, exalting the Almighty, constantly do they recount the honour of God and His holiness. Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, for the glory of Thy handiwork, and for the radiant lights that Thou hast made, they shall glorify Thee, Selah.",
                "page_start": false
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "conditions": [
        {
          "type": "opensiddur:holiday-aggregate",
          "features": {
            "shabbat": false
